/*
 * childop.def -- single-source registry of every childop.
 *
 * One CHILDOP() row per op; consumers #define CHILDOP before
 * #include-ing this file to expand the rows into an enum, the
 * dispatch table, the string-name lookup, the outer-KCOV-bracket
 * eligibility switch, and the picker slot-table / dormant-gate
 * arrays in child-altop-pick.c.
 *
 * Fields:
 *   enum_name           -- fully qualified enum tag (CHILD_OP_*)
 *   name_string         -- string form emitted by alt_op_name(); also
 *                          the token parsed by --canary-seed
 *   dispatch_fn         -- function of signature
 *                            bool fn(struct childdata *)
 *                          or NULL for ops handled off-dispatcher
 *                          (CHILD_OP_SYSCALL falls through to the
 *                          sequence-chain fast path)
 *   uses_outer_bracket  -- true iff the op's dispatch shape can carry
 *                          the per-call outer KCOV bracket that
 *                          publishes childop_edges_clean[op].  false
 *                          for CHILD_OP_SYSCALL (per-syscall internal
 *                          bracket) and CHILD_OP_SCHED_CYCLER (tight
 *                          loop over random_syscall would double-call
 *                          ioctl(KCOV_ENABLE)).
 *   dormant_default     -- initial value stored in the picker's
 *                          dormant_op_disabled[] slot for this op:
 *                          1 means "gated off until the canary queue
 *                          promotes it", 0 means "picker-eligible
 *                          from startup".  See dormant_op_set() /
 *                          canary_queue_tick() for the runtime flips.
 *
 * The row order is load-bearing: it defines the numeric value of
 * every CHILD_OP_* constant AND the slot ordering of the picker
 * arrays (pick_op_type_table[] / dormant_op_disabled[]) generated
 * out of this file.  Append new ops at the bottom; never reorder
 * existing rows.  Adding a new altop is a single-line edit here:
 * the enum, the picker slot, the dormant gate, the KCOV-bracket
 * predicate, and the dispatch-entry prototype in child-api.h all
 * pick it up on the next build.
 *
 * NO include guard -- this file is intended to be included multiple
 * times with different CHILDOP macro definitions.  Callers that
 * treat the sentinel row (CHILD_OP_SYSCALL, enum value 0) like any
 * other row can leave CHILDOP_SENTINEL undefined and get the
 * default expansion below; callers that need to exclude the
 * sentinel (e.g. the picker slot table, whose ARRAY_SIZE is
 * NR_CHILD_OP_TYPES - 1) redefine CHILDOP_SENTINEL to expand to
 * nothing before the #include.
 */

#ifndef CHILDOP_SENTINEL
#define CHILDOP_SENTINEL(enum_name, name_string) \
	CHILDOP(enum_name, name_string, NULL, false, 0)
#define _CHILDOP_SENTINEL_DEFAULT
#endif

CHILDOP_SENTINEL(CHILD_OP_SYSCALL, "syscall")
CHILDOP(CHILD_OP_MMAP_LIFECYCLE           , "mmap_lifecycle"             , mmap_lifecycle             , true, 0)
